{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Half of it.</b> \"Ah\" — a word a person says when he experiences pleasure. Like it: \"Ah, our eyes have seen\" (Isaiah 35:21 — but see note)." "<b>I have seen light.</b> Like \"light for him in Zion\" (Isaiah 30:9 — but see note)." "<b>I have seen.</b> According to its plain sense. And R. Saadia [said?] that its meaning is רָוַחְתִּי (I was relieved), without evil."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 44, :notes {0 "The verse cited as שם ל\"ה כ\"א does not match Isaiah 35:21, whose content does not contain this phrase; the citation may be erroneous or refer to a different passage.", 1 "Isaiah 30:9 does not contain this phrase; the citation appears erroneous or refers to a different verse."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:58:00.199570550Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}